# IMPORTANT — this file is NOT a second line of defence for `files`.
#
# When package.json sets `files`, npm uses that allowlist and .npmignore REPLACES
# the default ignore list rather than intersecting with it. Verified empirically:
# with files:["lib","scripts/*.py"] and .npmignore containing "lib/", npm packed
# lib/ anyway. So a bad entry in `files` cannot be corrected here.
#
# The control that actually matters is the `files` allowlist in package.json. This
# file is kept for the case where a package is packed WITHOUT `files`, and as
# documentation of what must never be published.
#
# Why the distinction matters: `files: ["scripts"]` (the original value) shipped
# the whole directory including scripts/__pycache__/*.pyc, which bake the build
# machine's absolute paths into the tarball. That was fixed by narrowing `files`.

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Maintainer-only scripts: they describe the author's own layout (the master
# sources, the vendoring flow) and are not needed to run the plugin.
tools/

# Test and audit artefacts
_survey*.txt
*.log

# User data that must never be published, even if present locally
*.enl
*.enlx
*.eni
*.Data/
library.db
library.db-*
*.enw
*.pdf
oa-inbox/
endnote-staging/
endnote-backups/
endnote.json
